   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia provided technical assistance to Tuvalu&#x2019;s Ministry of Finance to develop its five-year Public Financial Management (PFM) Roadmap, a critical step towards more accountable and inclusive governance.  Co-developed with government ministries, the roadmap ensures national ownership of reforms and aligns with Te Kete, Tuvalu&#x2019;s National Development Strategy.  It outlines key priorities including improved financial reporting, digitized procurement, expanded audit training, and streamlined revenue collections. These reforms directly respond to recommendations identified in the Assessment of National Systems and will guide Australia&#x2019;s ongoing support to Tuvalu through the Te Ao Program, including budget support.  The PFM Roadmap was approved by the Cabinet in July 2025. Australia stands ready to support its implementation through long-term capacity development and targeted use of local expertise, helping ensure reforms are both sustainable and locally led.  
&#x200d;
Through Te Ao, Australia&#x2019;s technical assistance also supported Tuvalu to produce its first-ever Citizen Budget, 18 months ahead of schedule. This milestone enhances public financial transparency, makes budget information more accessible and understandable for citizens, and strengthens both accountability and inclusion. It also fulfilled a trigger for multilateral budget support.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia provided technical assistance to Tuvalu&#x2019;s Ministry of Public Works and Infrastructure to strengthen the design and delivery of sustainable and climate resilient infrastructure.  This support enabled the Government of Tuvalu to complete a review of the national Building Code.   
&#x200d;
On 5 December 2024, Cabinet endorsed the Tuvalu National Building Code (Amendment 1).  The revised Code enhances disaster resilience by incorporating new sea-flood mapping data and resolving previous regulatory inconsistencies. This milestone also triggered one of the prerequisites for a General Budget Support tranche from the World Bank in 2025, boosting Tuvalu&#x2019;s financial resources. Australia continues to support Tuvalu in implementing the revised Code through ongoing technical assistance and capacity development of local staff for enforcement.  This ensures the safety and general welfare of the public and long-term functionality and resilience of the new buildings in Tuvalu.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
